  "notes": "Single flattened asset set. All listed graphics are copied into Assets/OurTaiko/Art; no runtime skin lookup or fallback. Song select / result: Nijiiro graphics and sounds copied unchanged; clear/fail/full-combo result voices are missing from Nijiiro and copied from PyTaikoGreen. Scripts/anim/*.lua exported timelines are kept verbatim as Assets/OurTaiko/Animations/*.txt and read by LumenClip (data only, no Lua runtime). Play options: the 21 Nijiiro hit-sound sets are copied as Assets/OurTaiko/Audio/hit_sounds/<index>/don.ogg and ka.ogg; their names from neiro_list.txt are stored in Generated/HitSounds.asset. Song loading curtain: global/rainbow_transition graphics and anim/loading_song.lua copied unchanged from Nijiiro. Nameplate: global/nameplate graphics (1P badge, plate, band, dan chips) copied unchanged from Nijiiro; the 2P and AI plates are not imported. Entry: Nijiiro entry background / credit / mode-board art and global timer, control-guide (indicator) and overlay chips copied unchanged (only the frames drawn: offline chip frame 0, the 演奏ゲーム board on/off/flash frames); entry sounds and the entry anim exports (entry_bg, credit_row, credit_fade, credit_side, mode_board) copied as .txt. entry/global/player_entry_* are fully transparent 8x8 placeholders and are not imported. Combo: game/combo counter, caption, gleam and 1P announce art copied unchanged from Nijiiro; the 1P combo voices 50 and 100-5000 (every 100) are copied to Assets/OurTaiko/Audio/combo; the 2P set is not imported. Judge counter: game/judge_counter/panel.png and bar.png are not skin art; ProjectBuilder.GenerateJudgeCounterArt draws them (colours sampled from the user's arcade reference). Its 良/可/不可/連打数 labels are cut from the imported result/score/max_combo_ja.png. Settings: Nijiiro has no settings art of its own (it inherits PyTaikoGreen's), so GlobalSettingScene uses PyTaikoGreen's settings background, footer, overlay, title, box, option buttons, blue arrow and BGM copied unchanged (1280-wide art drawn at 1.5x). ScoreRank: seven shared icon prefabs use the original result rank shapes; SongSelect resizes this same artwork. No yellow_box rank artwork is imported. The two rank_result frame tables are read as data by C# for the result animation; no Lua runtime.",
